msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-eval.md:22
msgid "Evaluate a Nix expression to JSON:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-eval.md:24
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"# nix eval --json --expr '{ x = 1; }'\n"
"{\"x\":1}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-eval.md:29
msgid "Evaluate a Nix expression from a file:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-eval.md:35
msgid "Get the current version of the `nixpkgs` flake:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-eval.md:41
msgid "Print the store path of the Hello package:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-eval.md:47
msgid "Get a list of checks in the `nix` flake:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-eval.md:53
msgid "Generate a directory with the specified contents:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-eval.md:55
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"# nix eval --write-to ./out --expr '{ foo = \"bar\"; subdir.bla = "
"\"123\"; }'\n"
"# cat ./out/foo\n"
"bar\n"
"# cat ./out/subdir/bla\n"
"123\n"
"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-eval.md:62
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-eval.md:64
msgid ""
"This command evaluates the given Nix expression, and prints the result on "
"standard output."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-eval.md:66
msgid "It also evaluates any nested attribute values and list items."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-eval.md:68
msgid "Output format"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-eval.md:70
msgid "`nix eval` can produce output in several formats:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-eval.md:72
msgid "By default, the evaluation result is printed as a Nix expression."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-eval.md:74
msgid ""
"With `--json`, the evaluation result is printed in JSON format. Note that "
"this fails if the result contains values that are not representable as JSON, "
"such as functions."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-eval.md:78
msgid ""
"With `--raw`, the evaluation result must be a string, which is printed "
"verbatim, without any quoting."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-eval.md:81
msgid ""
"With `--write-to` _path_, the evaluation result must be a string or a nested "
"attribute set whose leaf values are strings. These strings are written to "
"files named _path_/_attrpath_. _path_ must not already exist."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-eval.md:86
msgid "Options"
msgstr ""

